PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Your body is absorbing too much iron from your diet and storing it in your organs. It has damaged your liver (causing the swelling), your joints (causing the pain), your skin (causing the bronze color), and your pancreas, which has suddenly stopped producing insulin, resulting in your dangerously high blood sugar tonight. The hospital will immediately treat the high blood sugar with insulin and fluids before planning how to remove the excess iron.
Actionable Steps: Inform the admitting doctors immediately about the specific joint pain in your hands and the skin changes, as these are the crucial clues that will direct them to check your iron levels and genetics immediately, rather than just treating the high blood sugar in isolation.

